From: Sobs <antohasobne@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 16:22:35 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] engine: bare_app platform: frames and gamepad over bare_app's
 game_ipc.h

bare_app (a launcher for handheld consoles) starts its games with a socket
and shared memory with three frames of its video layer (its
src/games/game_ipc.h). --enable-bare-app=<bare_app's src> builds an engine
without SDL for it: the software renderer draws into the frame the engine
owns and swaps it with the middle one; with EGL the OpenGL ES renderers
draw off screen into a pbuffer on Mesa's surfaceless platform (the GPU's
render node), read back into that frame. The socket brings the gamepad's
buttons and axes (D-pad repeated in menus), sound goes to ALSA
(platform/linux/s_alsa.c, -alsadev). SIGTERM quits from the main loop so
that the settings are written; gl_vsync is kept off: there is no vsync, the
frame rate is fps_max.
